import Eval.Basic

/-!
# My first study

Use this file (or a copy of it) to formalize a claim from a paper you know.
Your agent can do most of the Lean writing. Your job is to check that each formal
statement says what the paper says.

For each claim, keep three things together, as in the template below:

1. The source: author, year, page, and the passage being formalized, quoted.
2. The claim in plain words.
3. The Lean statement and its proof.

A claim counts as checked by a person only after you have compared (2) and (3) with
(1) yourself. Record that with `Status: checked by <name>, <date>`.
-/

namespace MyProject.MyFirstStudy

/-
## Claim 1

Source: <Author (Year), p. N: "quoted passage">
In words: <the claim in plain language>
Status: not yet checked by a person

theorem claim1 : <Lean statement> := by
  <proof>
-/

end MyProject.MyFirstStudy
